{
	"name": "Abstracting Strike",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/skills/melee/strike-weapon-polearm-ice-blue.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Beginning at 7th level, your strikes are capable of disorienting your foes beyond simply being rattled or stunned. When you hit with a melee weapon attack, the target creature must succeed on a Constitution saving throw versus your maneuver DC. On a failure, the creature begins to see double. You gain one duplicate (as in the spell @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.Item.05w9nzp0kvu94k3h]{Mirror Image}) that persists for a number of rounds equal to your Charisma modifier. This duplicate has the same statistics as that granted by the spell, and dispels as normal when it takes damage.</p><p>At 13th level you gain 2 duplicates, and at 17th level you gain 3. Once you have used this ability, you cannot do so again until you complete a long rest.</p>",
